## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 via npm
- Added dependency to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with new package and dependencies

**2. Code Changes**
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`

### Implementation Details

Since this is a Next.js project using the App Router (indicated by the presence of `src/app/layout.tsx`), I followed the App Router-specific instructions from the Vercel documentation:
- The Analytics component is added to the root layout file
- Placed after the children content in the body element
- Uses the Next.js-specific import path `@vercel/analytics/next`

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linting and type checking passed (included in Next.js build)
✅ All dependencies properly installed
✅ Lock file updated correctly

### Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. Analytics will automatically start tracking visitors and page views after deployment

### Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

All changes preserve the existing code structure and follow Next.js best practices.
